From: Ruohang Feng <rh@vonng.com>
Date: Sat, 1 Aug 2026 17:00:00 +0800
Subject: Fix zero-radius GEOSEARCH on GCC 8 aarch64

Origin: vendor
Bug: https://github.com/valkey-io/valkey/issues/2051
Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-08-01

GCC 8 on aarch64 contracts the latitude conversion and subtraction into
an FMA sequence. Even when both latitude inputs are bit-identical, this can
produce a tiny non-zero distance and exclude the source member from a
zero-radius GEOSEARCH. Return the mathematically exact result before the
floating-point conversion.
---
 src/geohash_helper.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/src/geohash_helper.c b/src/geohash_helper.c
--- a/src/geohash_helper.c
+++ b/src/geohash_helper.c
@@ -282,5 +282,6 @@ GeoHashFix52Bits geohashAlign52Bits(const GeoHashBits hash) {
  * we can simplify arcsin(sin(x)) to x.
  */
 double geohashGetLatDistance(double lat1d, double lat2d) {
+    if (lat1d == lat2d) return 0.0;
     return EARTH_RADIUS_IN_METERS * fabs(deg_rad(lat2d) - deg_rad(lat1d));
 }
